        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0231" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg181"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McKinney to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    further correspondence in regard to the boundary question between Colombia and
                    Costa Rica.</p>
                <p>The Colombian minister of foreign affairs is opposed to the appointment of a
                    Colombian or Costa Rican legation to treat about the matter on account of the
                    expense.</p>
                <p>He sees no reason why the legations of their respective countries, at either
                    Washington or Madrid, should not arrange this matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Luther F.
                    McKinney.</hi></signed></closer>






